    },
    {
      "content": "In debate, I tend to be frank and constructive. I prefer scenario-based and operational reasoning, and I look for evidence from postmortems, benchmarks, and real capacity constraints. I become skeptical when proposals rely on hand-wavy planning, unowned risks, or tooling that performs confidence without improving reliability.",
      "title": "Debate style"
